          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A PHC medical officer is planning communicable disease prevention activities for</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A PHC medical officer is planning communicable disease prevention activities for her block. Which of the following is a PRIMARY prevention measure?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Sputum smear examination for TB suspects</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Sputum smear examination is a secondary prevention measure — it aims at early detection of existing disease, not prevention of occurrence.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Conducting routine immunisation under the UIP</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. Immunisation under the Universal Immunisation Programme prevents disease occurrence in susceptible individuals, which is the defining goal of primary prevention.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Contact tracing of confirmed tuberculosis cases</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Contact tracing is a secondary prevention measure — it identifies exposed individuals for early detection, not prevention of initial exposure.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Disability limitation in leprosy patients</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Disability limitation is a tertiary prevention measure, aimed at reducing the impact and complications of already-established disease.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Primary prevention aims to prevent disease occurrence in susceptible individuals. Immunisation under the UIP, sanitation, and vector control are primary prevention; early detection and treatment are secondary; disability limitation is tertiary."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Exactly right. Primary prevention aims to prevent disease occurrence — immunisation, sanitation, safe water supply, and vector control are the key PHC-level primary prevention activities."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
