          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A febrile patient presents to a PHC in a malaria-endemic district of Odisha duri</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A febrile patient presents to a PHC in a malaria-endemic district of Odisha during the monsoon. Which PHC-level diagnostic test should the medical officer order first?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>NS1 antigen test</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NS1 antigen is the first-line PHC test for suspected dengue within the first five days of fever. In a malaria-endemic area, malaria must be excluded first with a rapid diagnostic test.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Rapid Diagnostic Test (RDT) for malaria</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. In a malaria-endemic area, the RDT is the appropriate first-line PHC investigation for febrile patients, enabling prompt diagnosis and treatment to prevent severe complications.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>CBNAAT (GeneXpert)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>CBNAAT is used for rapid molecular diagnosis of tuberculosis in sputum samples, not as a first-line test for acute febrile illness.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Blood culture and sensitivity</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Blood culture is typically a district laboratory-level investigation, not a first-line PHC test. In an endemic area, a rapid diagnostic test for malaria is the immediate priority.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "In a malaria-endemic area, the Rapid Diagnostic Test (RDT) is the first-line PHC investigation for febrile patients. Matching the right test to the epidemiological context is a core skill for the primary care physician."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! Clinical vigilance plus appropriate PHC-level testing — RDT for malaria, sputum smear/CBNAAT for TB, NS1 for dengue — is the foundation of the primary care physician's detection role."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
